From: steinmarder W11 cs-observer track
Subject: [PATCH 8/N] drm/radeon: wire ib_chunk_pre_parse observer hook

Wires the ib_chunk_pre_parse observer hook.  Inserts a call to
radeon_palm_cs_observer_emit_ib_chunk_pre_parse(&parser) immediately
before radeon_cs_parser_relocs in radeon_cs_ioctl.  At this hook
point radeon_cs_parser_init has completed, so every chunk in
parser->chunks[] has been copy_from_user'd into kernel memory and
is safe to dereference without an additional copy.

Stub body in radeon_palm_cs_observer.c emits one
ib_chunk_pre_parse JSONL row PER CHUNK.  For each chunk:

  - chunk_index, chunk_id, length_dw, crc32_le of full chunk
  - first up-to-64 dwords as hex strings

Sized at 1536 bytes on the kernel stack (well under the 16 KiB
ceiling); no allocation on the emit path.  crc32_le is the
linux/crc32.h kernel helper, cheap O(n) over chunk bytes, suitable
for collision-resistant fingerprinting at byte-comparison scale.
Userspace can recompute SHA-256 of the same bytes from the JSONL
output for cryptographic-strength claims (the byte-path verdict decoder consumes this output).

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.7)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c
@@ -340,6 +340,8 @@
 		return r;
 	}

+	radeon_palm_cs_observer_emit_ib_chunk_pre_parse(&parser);
+
 	r = radeon_cs_parser_relocs(&parser);
 	if (r) {
 		if (r != -ERESTARTSYS)
